## 3. How to Run in ANSYS

### Option A — Open in ANSYS Workbench (GUI)
{% if wbpj_filename %}
1. Double-click **`{{ wbpj_filename }}`** in ANSYS Workbench.
2. Open **Mesh / Fluent** or run `fluent_meshing.jou` inside Fluent.
{% else %}
Run in Workbench:
```cmd
"{{ runwb2_hint }}" -B -R create_project.wbjn
```
{% endif %}

### Option B — Fully Automated Fluent Run (Zero Extra Setup)
Using stock ANSYS Fluent's built-in Python (`-py`):
```bash
fluent 3ddp -meshing -g -t{{ flight.cores }} -py -i run_fluent.py
```
Or with standalone `ansys-fluent-core` (`pip install -e ".[fluent]"`):
```bash
python run_fluent.py{% if mesh_conv.enabled %} --mesh-conv{% endif %}
```
*(Pass `--mesh-conv` / `--no-mesh-conv` or `ORK2CFD_MESH_SCALE=<factor>` to sweep or override spatial mesh density while keeping $y^+$ $\Delta y_1$ fixed.)*

### Option C — Classic Fluent TUI Journals (Workstation or HPC)
```bash
fluent 3ddp -meshing -g -t{{ flight.cores }} -i fluent_meshing.jou
fluent 3ddp -g -t{{ flight.cores }} -i fluent_solver.jou
```

